#!/bin/sh
#
# Configured as part of the DigitalOcean 1-Click Image build process

myip=$(hostname -I | awk '{print$1}')
cat <<EOF
********************************************************************************

Welcome to DigitalOcean's One-Click Coolify Droplet.

Coolify is an open-source, self-hostable platform that simplifies deploying and
managing applications, databases, and services on your own server. It's an
alternative to Heroku, Netlify, and Vercel that you control completely.

To access Coolify:
  Web Interface: http://$myip:8000

IMPORTANT FIRST STEPS:
  1. Visit http://$myip:8000 in your browser
  2. Create your admin account IMMEDIATELY
  3. The first user to register gets full admin access

Localhost SSH (verified on first boot when possible):
  - First boot attempts/verifies localhost SSH trust (Validate uses port 22)
  - Coolify UI is :8000 — do not set Servers → SSH port to 8000 or 8080
  - If localhost is Unavailable / Permission denied (publickey), or first-login
    says trust was not verified, run:
      /opt/configure-coolify-localhost.sh
    then Validate again with SSH port 22
  - If Validate times out on port 8080: set SSH port to 22, then re-validate

Management Commands:
  Start Coolify:    /opt/start-coolify.sh
  Stop Coolify:     /opt/stop-coolify.sh
  Restart Coolify:  /opt/restart-coolify.sh
  Update Coolify:   /opt/update-coolify.sh
  View logs:        /opt/coolify-logs.sh
  Check status:     /opt/coolify-status.sh
  Repair localhost: /opt/configure-coolify-localhost.sh

Using systemctl:
  Start:   systemctl start coolify
  Stop:    systemctl stop coolify
  Restart: systemctl restart coolify
  Status:  systemctl status coolify

On the server:
  Configuration:    /data/coolify/source/.env
  Main directory:   /data/coolify
  Applications:     /data/coolify/applications
  Databases:        /data/coolify/databases
  SSH keys:         /data/coolify/ssh/keys

Security & Firewall:
  UFW firewall is enabled with these open ports:
    - 22 (SSH — localhost Validate uses this)
    - 80 (HTTP)
    - 443 (HTTPS)
    - 8000 (Coolify Web Interface)
    - 6001 (Coolify Realtime)
    - 6002 (Coolify Soketi)

Next Steps:
  1. Set up your admin account at http://$myip:8000
  2. Confirm Servers → localhost → SSH port is 22, then Validate
  3. If Validate fails, run /opt/configure-coolify-localhost.sh and retry
  4. (Optional) Configure a custom domain for HTTPS
  5. Start deploying your applications!

For detailed documentation, visit: https://coolify.io/docs
For support, join the community: https://coolify.io/discord

********************************************************************************
To delete this message of the day: rm -rf $(readlink -f ${0})
EOF
